    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, boasting a standout 78.62 efficiency score. The combination of an elite batting order spot (#3) and a favorable matchup against Keller (xERA 4.26) positions **Corbin Carroll** as our primary source of speed and runs today. Close behind him are **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), both of whom benefit significantly from high-leverage lineup slots and park factors that favor their profiles. **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from an impressive 14% boost due to a dynamic platoon advantage against Scott, making him a high-floor start for Roto managers hunting for counting stats. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a rock-solid anchor at 1B with a 71.67 score, capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Cecconi.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning was keeping **Jose Caballero** on the bench. While his underlying metrics against left-handed pitching are strong, the hard constraint of our daily game caps and the current absence of a confirmed start forced him into the sub-40 bin. We are prioritizing players like **Tyler Soderstrom**\u2014who at 63.50 offers a cleaner path to production\u2014to ensure we maximize our limited roster moves. We are closely monitoring **Trevor Story** as the primary risk factor today; his score of 50.38 is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite arm in Jax (3.02 xERA), and any further news regarding his lineup status or health may lead us to pull the trigger on a swap with **Austin Riley** or **Giancarlo Stanton** if the latter are confirmed. \n\nManagers should remain alert regarding the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, and **Zach McKinstry**, as rotation in the middle infield remains a fluid situation. With **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki** all unavailable due to scheduled off-days or rest, our bench depth is intentionally thin to preserve efficiency. Prospect arms like **Dalton Rushing**, **Luis Campusano**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young** remain stashed in the wings, but today\u2019s tactical objective is clear: ride the speed of **Corbin Carroll** and the platoon advantages of **Mickey Moniak** to gain ground in the 5x5 standings. Keep a close watch on pre-game weather, as any delays could impact the high-ceiling outlook for our outfield trio.",
